excerpt: >-
  Embedded software development requires careful integration of hardware
  constraints, safety considerations, and real-time performance. Converent is
  fluent in architecture and implementation across bare‑metal and RTOS
  environments, with hands‑on delivery experience in model‑based and hand‑coded
  C development on TI, Infineon, and Microchip platforms. This foundation in
  proven development methods positions Converent to effectively apply emerging
  AI‑driven toolchains, ensuring generated outcomes remain verifiable, robust,
  and fit for purpose in safety‑critical systems.
---
Converent supports teams building safety-relevant and mission-critical embedded software with disciplined development practices, clear interfaces to hardware and systems models, and evidence that stands up to review.

Whether you need bring-up support, refactoring for maintainability, or alignment with functional safety and MBSE workflows, we work alongside your engineers to ship firmware you can trust in the field.
